==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ang}} {{term|deadlic|dēadlīċ}} (adj.), {{term|deadlice|dēadlīċe}} (adv.), corresponding to {{suffix|dead|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈdɛdli/}}
* {{audio|en-us-deadly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|deadli|er|more}}

# {{obsolete}} Subject to [[death]]; [[mortal]].
#* '''1485''', Sir Thomas Malory, ''Le Morte Darthur'', Book XVII:
#*: And than he began to tremble ryght harde whan the '''dedly''' fleysh began to beholde the spirituall thynges. 
# Causing death; [[lethal]].
# {{context|by extension}} very [[accurate]] (of aiming with a bow, firearm, etc.)
# {{informal}} very [[boring]]
# {{informal}} [[excellent]], [[awesome]], [[cool]]

